    <title>NanoTekSpice</title>
    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><anchor id="md__r_e_a_d_m_e_1autotoc_md0"/></para>
<sect1 id="md__r_e_a_d_m_e_1autotoc_md1">
<title>Overview</title><para><bold>NanoTekSpice</bold> is a digital logic simulator built in <bold>C++</bold>^^. <bold>It constructs a graph of simulated digital electronic components (chipsets) based on a configuration file and simulates their behavior using boolean logic</bold>^^. <bold>Unlike pure boolean algebra, this simulator incorporates a ****tristate logic</bold> system, accounting for <computeroutput>&lt;span class="citation-47"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>&lt;span class="citation-47"&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>&lt;span class="citation-47"&gt;undefined&lt;/span&gt;</computeroutput> states^^.</para>
<para><bold>The project simulates various components ranging from simple elementary gates (AND, OR, NOT) to complex chipsets like the 4008 4-bit adder or the 4514 4-bit decoder</bold>.</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="md__r_e_a_d_m_e_1autotoc_md3">
<title>Features</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>Tristate Logic:</bold> Handles <computeroutput>&lt;span class="citation-45"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;</computeroutput> (false), <computeroutput>&lt;span class="citation-45"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;</computeroutput> (true), and <computeroutput>&lt;span class="citation-45"&gt;U&lt;/span&gt;</computeroutput> (undefined) values.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Component Factory:</bold> Implements a generic component creation system using a factory pattern.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Interactive Shell:</bold> Includes a command-line interface to manipulate input values, simulate clock ticks, and display the state of the circuit.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Modular Architecture:</bold> All components inherit from the <computeroutput>&lt;span class="citation-42"&gt;<ref refid="classnts_1_1_i_component" kindref="compound">nts::IComponent</ref>&lt;/span&gt;</computeroutput> interface, ensuring high extensibility.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="md__r_e_a_d_m_e_1autotoc_md5">
<title>Getting Started</title><sect2 id="md__r_e_a_d_m_e_1autotoc_md6">
<title>Prerequisites</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><bold>A C++ compiler (supporting C++ standards used in the project)</bold>^^.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>Make</bold> or <bold>CMake</bold> for the build process^^.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</sect2>
<sect2 id="md__r_e_a_d_m_e_1autotoc_md7">
<title>Compilation</title><para>To compile the project using the provided <bold>Makefile</bold> , run the following commands in your terminal:</para>
<para><bold>Bash</bold></para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">#<sp/>To<sp/>compile<sp/>the<sp/>nanotekspice<sp/>binary</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">make</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">#<sp/>To<sp/>remove<sp/>object<sp/>files</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">make<sp/>clean</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">#<sp/>To<sp/>remove<sp/>object<sp/>files<sp/>and<sp/>the<sp/>binary</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">make<sp/>fclean</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">#<sp/>To<sp/>re-compile<sp/>the<sp/>entire<sp/>project</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">make<sp/>re</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect2>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="md__r_e_a_d_m_e_1autotoc_md9">
<title>Usage</title><para>Run the simulator by passing a circuit configuration file (<computeroutput>.<ref refid="namespacents" kindref="compound">nts</ref></computeroutput>) as an argument:</para>
<para><bold>Bash</bold></para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">./nanotekspice<sp/>[circuit_file.nts]</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<sect2 id="md__r_e_a_d_m_e_1autotoc_md10">
<title>Available Commands</title><para>Once the program is running, you can use the following commands in the interactive prompt:</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>**<computeroutput>&lt;span class="citation-37"&gt;display&lt;/span&gt;</computeroutput>** <bold>: Prints the current tick and the values of all inputs and outputs</bold>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>**<computeroutput>&lt;span class="citation-36"&gt;simulate&lt;/span&gt;</computeroutput>** <bold>: Simulates one tick of the circuit</bold>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>**<computeroutput>&lt;span class="citation-35"&gt;loop&lt;/span&gt;</computeroutput>** **: Continuously runs the simulation until a **<computeroutput>&lt;span class="citation-35"&gt;SIGINT&lt;/span&gt;</computeroutput> (CTRL+C) is received^^.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>**<computeroutput>&lt;span class="citation-34"&gt;[input_name]=[value]&lt;/span&gt;</computeroutput>** **: Changes the value of an input (values: **<computeroutput>&lt;span class="citation-34"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>&lt;span class="citation-34"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;</computeroutput>, or <computeroutput>&lt;span class="citation-34"&gt;u&lt;/span&gt;</computeroutput>).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>**<computeroutput>&lt;span class="citation-33"&gt;exit&lt;/span&gt;</computeroutput>** <bold>: Closes the program</bold>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><bold>CTRL+D</bold> <bold>: Stops the program with status 0</bold>.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect2>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="md__r_e_a_d_m_e_1autotoc_md12">
<title>Configuration File Format</title><para>The <computeroutput>.<ref refid="namespacents" kindref="compound">nts</ref></computeroutput> files are divided into two main sections:</para>
<para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para>**<computeroutput>&lt;span class="citation-31"&gt;.chipsets&lt;/span&gt;</computeroutput>** <bold>: Declares and names the components used in the circuit</bold>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>**<computeroutput>&lt;span class="citation-30"&gt;.links&lt;/span&gt;</computeroutput>** <bold>: Defines the bidirectional links between specific pins of the components</bold>.</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para><bold>Example:</bold></para>
<para><bold>Plaintext</bold></para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">.chipsets:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">input<sp/>a</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">input<sp/>b</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">4071<sp/>my_or_gate</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">output<sp/>s</highlight></codeline>
<codeline></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">.links:</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">a:1<sp/>my_or_gate:1</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">b:1<sp/>my_or_gate:2</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">my_or_gate:3<sp/>s:1</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
</sect1>
<sect1 id="md__r_e_a_d_m_e_1autotoc_md14">
